tmp.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco Compute Hyperconverged C220 M6 and C240 M6 through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "info", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type": "eolAdvisory", "Version": "1.0", "Workaround": "", "account_name": "MAPLE", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:16:46.039Z"}
{"AccountMoid": "5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "Actions": [{"AffectedObjectType": "compute.RackUnit", "AlertType": "eolAdvisory", "Identifiers": [{"Name": "Moid", "ObjectType": "tam.Identifiers", "Value": "ds1_Moid"}], "Name": "", "ObjectType": "tam.Action", "OperationType": "create", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds2", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT * FROM ds1 where ( datediff(current_date(), '2030-09-30' ) >= 0 )"}], "Type": "restApi"}], "AdvisoryDetails": {"AllMilestones": [{"Date": "2030-09-30T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Date of (Hardware) Support", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}], "Description": "", "Milestone": {"Date": "2030-09-30T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "past", "MilestoneType": "lastDateOfSupport", "Name": "Last Date Of Support(LDOS) Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, "ObjectType": "tam.EolAdvisoryDetails", "Release": "C220 M6, C240 M6"}, "AdvisoryId": "ucs-m6-rack-ldos-critical", "Ancestors": [], "ApiDataSources": [{"MoType": "computePhysicalSummary", "Name": "ds1", "ObjectType": "tam.ApiDataSource", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds1", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT ds1_Moid, ds1_AccountMoid, ds1_DomainGroupMoid, ds1_RegisteredDevice.Moid as ds1_RegisteredDeviceMoid, ds1_Model, ds1_Personality FROM ds1 WHERE ds1_Model RLIKE '(UCSC.*C220.*M6|UCSC.*C240.*M6)'"}], "Type": "intersightApi"}], "CreateTime": "2025-05-01T19:31:36.252Z", "DatePublished": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z", "DateUpdated": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z", "Description": "Cisco announced the end-of-sale and end-of-life dates for the Cisco UCS C220 M6 and C240 M6 Rack Servers. The last date of (hardware) support for the affected product(s) was September 30, 2030.", "DomainGroupMoid": "5b2541877a7662743465cc89", "ExecuteOnPod": "tier1", "ExternalUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/hyperconverged-infrastructure/compute-hyperconverged-nutanix/compute-hyperconverged-c220-m6-c240-m6-eol.html", "ModTime": "2026-09-18T18:16:46.001Z", "Moid": "6813cc186f636b3901e86fb8", "Name": "Last Date of Support for the Cisco C220 M6 and C240 M6 is past", "ObjectType": "tam.AdvisoryDefinition", "Organization": {"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}, "OtherRefUrls": [], "Owners": ["5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "shared"], "PermissionResources": [{"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}], "Recommendation": "Customers may be able to use the Cisco Technology Migration Program (TMP) where applicable to trade-in eligible products and receive credit toward the purchase of new Cisco equipment. For more information about Cisco TMP, customers should work with their Cisco Partner or Cisco account team. Cisco Partners can find additional TMP information on Partner Central at [https://www.cisco.com/web/partners/incentives_and_promotions/tmp.html](https://www.cisco.com/web/partners/incentives_and_promotions/tmp.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco Compute Hyperconverged C220 M6 and C240 M6 through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "info", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type": "eolAdvisory", "Version": "1.0", "Workaround": "", "account_name": "MAPLE", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:16:46.001Z"}
{"AccountMoid": "5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "Actions": [{"AffectedObjectType": "compute.RackUnit", "AlertType": "eolAdvisory", "Identifiers": [{"Name": "Moid", "ObjectType": "tam.Identifiers", "Value": "ds1_Moid"}], "Name": "", "ObjectType": "tam.Action", "OperationType": "create", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds2", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT * FROM ds1 where ( datediff(current_date(), '2025-04-02' ) >= 0 )"}], "Type": "restApi"}], "AdvisoryDetails": {"AllMilestones": [{"Date": "2025-04-02T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The date the document that announces the end-of-sale and end-of-life of a product is distributed to the general public.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "End of Life Announcement Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2025-09-29T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to order the product through Cisco point-of-sale mechanisms. The product is no longer for sale after this date.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "End of Sale Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2025-12-28T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last-possible ship date that can be requested of Cisco and/or its contract manufacturers. Actual ship date is dependent on lead time.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Ship Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2026-09-29T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last-possible date a routine failure analysis may be performed to determine the cause of hardware product failure or defect.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "End of Routine Failure Analysis Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2026-09-29T00:00:00Z", "Description": "For equipment and software that is not covered by a service-and-support contract, this is the last date to order a new service-and-support contract or add the equipment and/or software to an existing service-and-support contract.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "End of New Service Attachment Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2029-12-25T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to extend or renew a service contract for the product.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "End of Service Contract Renewal Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, {"Date": "2030-09-30T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Date of (Hardware) Support", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}], "Description": "", "Milestone": {"Date": "2025-04-02T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The date the document that announces the end-of-sale and end-of-life of a product is distributed to the general public.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "info", "MilestoneType": "endOfLifeAnnouncementDate", "Name": "End of Life(EOL) Announcement Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, "ObjectType": "tam.EolAdvisoryDetails", "Release": "C220 M6, C240 M6"}, "AdvisoryId": "ucs-m6-rack-eol-info", "Ancestors": [], "ApiDataSources": [{"MoType": "computePhysicalSummary", "Name": "ds1", "ObjectType": "tam.ApiDataSource", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds1", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT ds1_Moid, ds1_AccountMoid, ds1_DomainGroupMoid, ds1_RegisteredDevice.Moid as ds1_RegisteredDeviceMoid, ds1_Model, ds1_Personality FROM ds1 WHERE ds1_Model RLIKE '(UCSC.*C220.*M6|UCSC.*C240.*M6)'"}], "Type": "intersightApi"}], "CreateTime": "2025-05-01T19:31:36.209Z", "DatePublished": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z", "DateUpdated": "2025-04-03T00:00:00Z", "Description": "Cisco announces the end-of-sale and end-of-life dates for the Cisco UCS C220 M6 and C240 M6 Rack Servers. The last day to order the affected product(s) is September 29, 2025. Customers with active service contracts will continue to receive support from the Cisco Technical Assistance Center (TAC) based on EoL bulletin.", "DomainGroupMoid": "5b2541877a7662743465cc89", "ExecuteOnPod": "tier1", "ExternalUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/servers-unified-computing/ucs-c-series-rack-servers/ucs-c220-m6-c240-rack-server-eol.html", "ModTime": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.969Z", "Moid": "6813cc186f636b3901e86fb3", "Name": "End-of-Sale and End-of-Life Announcement for the Cisco UCS C220 M6 and C240 M6 Rack Servers", "ObjectType": "tam.AdvisoryDefinition", "Organization": {"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}, "OtherRefUrls": [], "Owners": ["5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "shared"], "PermissionResources": [{"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}], "Recommendation": "Customers may be able to use the Cisco Technology Migration Program (TMP) where applicable to trade-in eligible products and receive credit toward the purchase of new Cisco equipment. For more information about Cisco TMP, customers should work with their Cisco Partner or Cisco account team. Cisco Partners can find additional TMP information on Partner Central at [https://www.cisco.com/web/partners/incentives_and_promotions/tmp.html](https://www.cisco.com/web/partners/incentives_and_promotions/tmp.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco UCS C220 M6 and C240 M6 Rack Servers through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/web/about/ac227/ac228/ac231/about_cisco_takeback_recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "info", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type": "eolAdvisory", "Version": "1.0", "Workaround": "", "account_name": "MAPLE", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.969Z"}
{"AccountMoid": "5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "Actions": [{"AffectedObjectType": "network.Element", "AlertType": "eolAdvisory", "Identifiers": [{"Name": "Moid", "ObjectType": "tam.Identifiers", "Value": "ds1_Moid"}], "Name": "", "ObjectType": "tam.Action", "OperationType": "create", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds2", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT * FROM ds1 where ( datediff(current_date(), '2031-12-31' ) >= -180 and datediff(current_date(), '2031-12-31' ) < -90 )"}], "Type": "restApi"}], "AdvisoryDetails": {"AllMilestones": [{"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Date of Support Hardware", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}], "Description": "", "Milestone": {"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": -90, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "lastDateOfSupport", "Name": "Last Date Of Support(LDOS) Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": -180}, "ObjectType": "tam.EolAdvisoryDetails", "Release": "UCS-FI-6454, UCS-FI-64108, UCSX-FI-6454, UCSX-FI-64108, HCI-FI-6454, HCI-FI-64108, HCIX-FI-6454, HCIX-FI-64108"}, "AdvisoryId": "ucs-fi-6400-ldos-upcoming", "Ancestors": [], "ApiDataSources": [{"MoType": "networkElementSummary", "Name": "ds1", "ObjectType": "tam.ApiDataSource", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds1", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT ds1_Moid, ds1_AccountMoid, ds1_DomainGroupMoid, ds1_RegisteredDevice.Moid as ds1_RegisteredDeviceMoid, ds1_Model FROM ds1 WHERE ds1_Model RLIKE '(UCS-FI-64|UCSX-FI-64|HCI-FI-64|HCIX-FI-64)' and ds1_SourceObjectType = 'network.Element'"}], "Type": "intersightApi"}], "CreateTime": "2026-07-07T10:59:11.561Z", "DatePublished": "2026-06-23T00:00:00Z", "DateUpdated": "2026-07-01T00:00:00Z", "Description": "Cisco announced the end-of-sale and end-of-life dates for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series. The last date of (hardware) support for the affected product(s) is December 31, 2031. Customers with active service contracts will continue to receive support from the Cisco Technical Assistance Center (TAC) based on EoL bulletin.", "DomainGroupMoid": "5b2541877a7662743465cc89", "ExecuteOnPod": "tier1", "ExternalUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/servers-unified-computing/ucs-6400-series-fabric-interconnects/fabric-interconnect-6400-series-eol.html", "ModTime": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.933Z", "Moid": "6a4cdbff6f636b3901ef37c5", "Name": "Last Date of Support for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series is upcoming", "ObjectType": "tam.AdvisoryDefinition", "Organization": {"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}, "OtherRefUrls": [], "Owners": ["5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "shared"], "PermissionResources": [{"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}], "Recommendation": "Customers currently running Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series should consider migrating to the 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnects:\n\n- **UCS-FI-6652-U** - 6th GEN UCS Fabric Interconnect 1RU 10/25/50G Eth, 64G FC\n- **UCS-FI-6664-U** - 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnect 2RU 100G Eth, 64G FC\n\nCustomers may be able to use the Cisco Takeback and Reuse Program where applicable to return hardware that has reached end-of-use, at no cost. Returned products are put to their next best use, whether reused, remanufactured, or recycled by one of Cisco's certified contracted recyclers. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "info", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type": "eolAdvisory", "Version": "1.0", "Workaround": "", "account_name": "MAPLE", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.933Z"}
{"AccountMoid": "5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "Actions": [{"AffectedObjectType": "network.Element", "AlertType": "eolAdvisory", "Identifiers": [{"Name": "Moid", "ObjectType": "tam.Identifiers", "Value": "ds1_Moid"}], "Name": "", "ObjectType": "tam.Action", "OperationType": "create", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds2", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT * FROM ds1 where ( datediff(current_date(), '2031-12-31' ) >= 0 )"}], "Type": "restApi"}], "AdvisoryDetails": {"AllMilestones": [{"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Date of Support Hardware", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}], "Description": "", "Milestone": {"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "past", "MilestoneType": "lastDateOfSupport", "Name": "Last Date Of Support(LDOS) Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}, "ObjectType": "tam.EolAdvisoryDetails", "Release": "UCS-FI-6454, UCS-FI-64108, UCSX-FI-6454, UCSX-FI-64108, HCI-FI-6454, HCI-FI-64108, HCIX-FI-6454, HCIX-FI-64108"}, "AdvisoryId": "ucs-fi-6400-ldos-past", "Ancestors": [], "ApiDataSources": [{"MoType": "networkElementSummary", "Name": "ds1", "ObjectType": "tam.ApiDataSource", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds1", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT ds1_Moid, ds1_AccountMoid, ds1_DomainGroupMoid, ds1_RegisteredDevice.Moid as ds1_RegisteredDeviceMoid, ds1_Model FROM ds1 WHERE ds1_Model RLIKE '(UCS-FI-64|UCSX-FI-64|HCI-FI-64|HCIX-FI-64)' and ds1_SourceObjectType = 'network.Element'"}], "Type": "intersightApi"}], "CreateTime": "2026-07-07T10:59:11.529Z", "DatePublished": "2026-06-23T00:00:00Z", "DateUpdated": "2026-07-01T00:00:00Z", "Description": "Cisco announced the end-of-sale and end-of-life dates for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series. The last date of (hardware) support for the affected product(s) was December 31, 2031.", "DomainGroupMoid": "5b2541877a7662743465cc89", "ExecuteOnPod": "tier1", "ExternalUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/servers-unified-computing/ucs-6400-series-fabric-interconnects/fabric-interconnect-6400-series-eol.html", "ModTime": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.899Z", "Moid": "6a4cdbff6f636b3901ef37c0", "Name": "Last Date of Support for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series is past", "ObjectType": "tam.AdvisoryDefinition", "Organization": {"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}, "OtherRefUrls": [], "Owners": ["5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "shared"], "PermissionResources": [{"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}], "Recommendation": "Customers currently running Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series should consider migrating to the 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnects:\n\n- **UCS-FI-6652-U** - 6th GEN UCS Fabric Interconnect 1RU 10/25/50G Eth, 64G FC\n- **UCS-FI-6664-U** - 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnect 2RU 100G Eth, 64G FC\n\nCustomers may be able to use the Cisco Takeback and Reuse Program where applicable to return hardware that has reached end-of-use, at no cost. Returned products are put to their next best use, whether reused, remanufactured, or recycled by one of Cisco's certified contracted recyclers. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "critical", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type": "eolAdvisory", "Version": "1.0", "Workaround": "", "account_name": "MAPLE", "updated_at": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.899Z"}
{"AccountMoid": "5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "Actions": [{"AffectedObjectType": "network.Element", "AlertType": "eolAdvisory", "Identifiers": [{"Name": "Moid", "ObjectType": "tam.Identifiers", "Value": "ds1_Moid"}], "Name": "", "ObjectType": "tam.Action", "OperationType": "create", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds2", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT * FROM ds1 where ( datediff(current_date(), '2031-12-31' ) >= -90 and datediff(current_date(), '2031-12-31' ) < -30 )"}], "Type": "restApi"}], "AdvisoryDetails": {"AllMilestones": [{"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": 2147483647, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "unknown", "Name": "Last Date of Support Hardware", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": 0}], "Description": "", "Milestone": {"Date": "2031-12-31T00:00:00Z", "Description": "The last date to receive applicable service and support for the product as entitled by active service contracts or by warranty terms and conditions. After this date, all support services for the product are unavailable, and the product becomes obsolete.", "EndOffset": -30, "LabelHint": "upcoming", "MilestoneType": "lastDateOfSupport", "Name": "Last Date Of Support(LDOS) Date", "ObjectType": "tam.Milestone", "StartOffset": -90}, "ObjectType": "tam.EolAdvisoryDetails", "Release": "UCS-FI-6454, UCS-FI-64108, UCSX-FI-6454, UCSX-FI-64108, HCI-FI-6454, HCI-FI-64108, HCIX-FI-6454, HCIX-FI-64108"}, "AdvisoryId": "ucs-fi-6400-ldos-medium", "Ancestors": [], "ApiDataSources": [{"MoType": "networkElementSummary", "Name": "ds1", "ObjectType": "tam.ApiDataSource", "Queries": [{"Name": "qds1", "ObjectType": "tam.QueryEntry", "Priority": 1, "Query": "SELECT ds1_Moid, ds1_AccountMoid, ds1_DomainGroupMoid, ds1_RegisteredDevice.Moid as ds1_RegisteredDeviceMoid, ds1_Model FROM ds1 WHERE ds1_Model RLIKE '(UCS-FI-64|UCSX-FI-64|HCI-FI-64|HCIX-FI-64)' and ds1_SourceObjectType = 'network.Element'"}], "Type": "intersightApi"}], "CreateTime": "2026-07-07T10:59:11.501Z", "DatePublished": "2026-06-23T00:00:00Z", "DateUpdated": "2026-07-01T00:00:00Z", "Description": "Cisco announced the end-of-sale and end-of-life dates for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series. The last date of (hardware) support for the affected product(s) is December 31, 2031. Customers with active service contracts will continue to receive support from the Cisco Technical Assistance Center (TAC) based on EoL bulletin.", "DomainGroupMoid": "5b2541877a7662743465cc89", "ExecuteOnPod": "tier1", "ExternalUrl": "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/collateral/servers-unified-computing/ucs-6400-series-fabric-interconnects/fabric-interconnect-6400-series-eol.html", "ModTime": "2026-09-18T18:16:45.872Z", "Moid": "6a4cdbff6f636b3901ef37ba", "Name": "Last Date of Support for the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series is upcoming", "ObjectType": "tam.AdvisoryDefinition", "Organization": {"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}, "OtherRefUrls": [], "Owners": ["5960901ca94eba000127e33a", "shared"], "PermissionResources": [{"Moid": "5dde9f896972652d3353a082", "ObjectType": "organization.Organization", "link": "https://intersight.com/api/v1/organization/Organizations/5dde9f896972652d3353a082"}], "Recommendation": "Customers currently running Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series should consider migrating to the 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnects:\n\n- **UCS-FI-6652-U** - 6th GEN UCS Fabric Interconnect 1RU 10/25/50G Eth, 64G FC\n- **UCS-FI-6664-U** - 6th Generation UCS Fabric Interconnect 2RU 100G Eth, 64G FC\n\nCustomers may be able to use the Cisco Takeback and Reuse Program where applicable to return hardware that has reached end-of-use, at no cost. Returned products are put to their next best use, whether reused, remanufactured, or recycled by one of Cisco's certified contracted recyclers. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse.html).\n\nCustomers may be able to continue to purchase the Cisco Fabric Interconnect 6400 Series through the Cisco Refresh (certified remanufactured) program. Remanufactured units may be available in limited supply for sale in certain countries on a first-come, first-served basis until the Last Date of Support has been reached. For information about the Cisco Refresh program, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/remanufactured.html).\n\nThe Cisco Takeback and Recycle program helps businesses properly dispose of surplus products that have reached their end of useful life. The program is open to all business users of Cisco equipment and its associated brands and subsidiaries. For more information, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/about/takeback-and-reuse/product-recycling.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco End-of-Life Policy, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/eos-eol-policy.html).\n\nFor more information about the Cisco Product Warranties, go to: [https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html](https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/products/warranty-listing.html).\n\nTo subscribe to receive end-of-life/end-of-sale information, go to: [https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications](https://cway.cisco.com/mynotifications).", "S3DataSources": [], "Severity": {"Level": "medium", "ObjectType": "tam.EolSeverity"}, "SharedScope": "shared", "State": "ready", "Tags": [], "Type